                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Another game claiming to make levels based on your MP3 files, but it's just another generic, clunky BPM tracking metronome game. Terrorrhythm is effectively One Finger Death Punch, but claims to be music based. The blueprint was RIGHT THERE!  Have enemies attack you on beats, half-beats, and quarter beats. It's not fucking hard! Nah man, we're gonna make you only able to attack on single beats, but swarm you with enemies that don't follow ANY spawning or attack patterns that are based on the MP3 track. Well, at least I don't have to manually input the BPM... EXCEPT YOU KINDA DO! What is the fucking point of this game? It's 100% blatantly false advertising.\n\nI'm effectively done with this entire genre. Just go get Melody's Escape 2. It's better, and actually works as advertised. Is it the same sub-genre? No, but it does what it says on the tin.",
